You probably already knew we had Lojbab and Nora, and John Woldemar
Cowan (author of the Complete Lojban Language). You probably knew
Lawrence Schoen of the Klingon Langauge Insitute will visit with us.

But did you know jbonunsla's registration numbers stand at 21 now?

Did you know eight of them are members or officers in the Logical
Language Group?

Did you know Dave Montenegro (brablonau) will present his new
slideshow presentation?

Did you know Arika Okrent, PhD (http://www.wickedoasis.org/arika/),
will speak on her
upcoming book about invented languages, and conduct a group interview
of us about the history of logical languages?

Holy cow, I am geeking out at this moment from the sheer awesomeness.
Who knows, maybe Philcon's Guest of Honor Charlie Stross will stop by
to chat (because I made him a Guest of Honor at Penguicon 2007).
That's sheer speculation, but I'm just thinking of how on earth
jbonunsla could get any better.

Oh yeah: I know how it could get better. You could join us! Hurry and
register before October 27 has come and gone. Instructions and details
are here: http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-index.php?page=jbonunsla+2006
